{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1106085-mayo-vs-mustard","id":1106085,"title":"Mayo vs Mustard","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-21T09:16:20-07:00","id":1106085,"title":"Mayo vs Mustard","content":"I bought all the Mage Ascension books back in my much younger days, but when Awakening came along I switched over to it because the inherent core of that line appealed more to me (exploring mysteries vs fighting a pointless fight for reality). I never hated Ascension, just thought it was firmly based in its time. I have recently started reading M20 and its associate books, partly out of nostalgia, but also out of curiosity as to how the game line might have evolved to better reflect the current zeitgeist.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhile reading the more balanced take on the main factions, it struck me that (in my mind) the difference between mayo lovers vs mustard lovers is kind of a good analogy for technocrats vs mystics. Mayo is bland and homogenous and appeals to a large group of people because of its utility and ability to add moisture/binding to what ever it is added to. Mustard tends to be have a large variety (spicy, yellow, brown, Dijon, honey, wholegrain, powder, ect.) and literally adds spice to whatever it is added to. Even when mayo tries to be more than it is meant to be (I'm looking at you chipotle mayo) it just trying to be more mustard like. Mustard usually fails if used as a binding/moisture agent because it overpowers when used that liberally.<br /> <br /> \u200bKind of sounds like technocrats vs mystics to me. Here's the thing, I am firmly a mustard lover, but mayo is too useful not to use in cooking. Ever tried adding moisture to a tuna salad with just mustard - not fun, so I use a small amount of mayo. I know plenty of mayo lovers that add a little mustard to their sandwiches along with their mayo for the spice.<br /> <br /> \u200bI like that some of the emphasis in M20 has shifted away from the use vs them of technocrats vs mystics and more towards holy crud the Nephandi have body snatched our leaders and that's how we got here because at the end of the day I will never put mayo on one of my sandwiches, but I don't have a problem if you want to.<br /> <br /> \u200bThanks for letting me ramble/muse...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3385-ckobbe","name":"ckobbe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T10:32:32-07:00","id":1106130,"title":"","content":"You may like Reality Zones. They allow you to have real gains for your effort in the war for reality, making it much less pointless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T10:55:18-07:00","id":1106143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ckobbe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1106085-mayo-vs-mustard#post1106085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI like that some of the emphasis in M20 has shifted away from the use vs them of technocrats vs mystics and more towards holy crud the Nephandi have body snatched our leaders</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this one of possible scenarios presented in M20 (and elsewhere) is that those leaders might be Nephandi, or influenced by the Nephandi, rather than being 'body snatched' by the Nephandi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T15:39:27-07:00","id":1106295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ckobbe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1106085-mayo-vs-mustard#post1106085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I never hated Ascension, just thought it was firmly based in its time. I have recently started reading M20 and its associate books, partly out of nostalgia, but also out of curiosity as to how the game line might have evolved to better reflect the current zeitgeist.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting thought. How'd you define the current zeitgeist and how Mage is out of sync with it? I'm asking this, because I came late to MtA (during the late 2000s) and stayed since and I never felt it's core out-of-time (specific minor elements, yes, but not he whole and not the important themes), but that could be just me and my worldview.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T08:11:56-07:00","id":1106559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1106085-mayo-vs-mustard?p=1106130#post1106130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You may like Reality Zones. They allow you to have real gains for your effort in the war for reality, making it much less pointless.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI've caught references to it, but haven't gotten to that specific section of the massive book yet, but a certain flexibility in the consensual reality has always been part of Ascension, so I'm sure I'll appreciate it.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso, to be clear, when I said pointless, I meant in the grand scheme of things, not in the individual or game level. A large part of the premise of the entire first run of White Wolf games and their meta-plots was a certain inevitability of an impending apocalypse. I had a lot a great games back in the day that were in no way pointless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3385-ckobbe","name":"ckobbe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T08:33:33-07:00","id":1106571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1106085-mayo-vs-mustard?p=1106295#post1106295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's an interesting thought. How'd you define the current zeitgeist and how Mage is out of sync with it? I'm asking this, because I came late to MtA (during the late 2000s) and stayed since and I never felt it's core out-of-time (specific minor elements, yes, but not he whole and not the important themes), but that could be just me and my worldview.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bAs I said in the previous post, there was a definite feel of impending doom/apocalypse to the original line, which was completely understandable with the upcoming turn of the millennium, and even later in 2012 with the end of the mayan calendar. With things like the Lance Henricksen show Millennium, Rapture themed works and other media feeding/tapping into the same zeitgeist. It seems so silly now, but there were serious concerns about the Y2K bug wiping out computer systems as we know it, as well as other general hysteria. If there was any doubt about these themes White Wolf finished off each line with their end of the world coda book.<br /> <br /> \u200bWe still have apocalyptic memes in media and our society, but they seem to have shifted from the world will end to society collapsing/stagnating.Things like the housing crisis and the failure of big banks have shifted a lot of peoples concerns to a much more personal level. It's hard to worry about the end of the world when you are worried about the next mortgage payment. Yet, with all that there are so many things that feel like progress (even if they are heavily resisted in various arenas) that don't seem tied to the rampant consumerism of the 90s. Forms of Democracy have gotten a second wind (and the hit again) with things like the Arab Spring, gender and sexuality equality are much better than when I was a kid (although they still have a long way to go), Captain America is black and Thor is a woman. Many YouTube stars are banal glory seekers, but so many others are able to artistically flourish in a way never before because they control the platform and their message. It is a very paradoxical time (no pun intended).<br /> <br /> \u200bOne of the reasons that I shifted to Awakening (which to be fair has far less weighty philosophical underpinnings than Ascension) was a desire to move away from the nihilism inherent in the original game line. What I have read so far of M20 seems to have shifted away from that, which I am thankful for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3385-ckobbe","name":"ckobbe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T16:05:32-07:00","id":1106760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ckobbe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1106085-mayo-vs-mustard?p=1106571#post1106571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bAs I said in the previous post, there was a definite feel of impending doom/apocalypse to the original line, which was completely understandable with the upcoming turn of the millennium, and even later in 2012 with the end of the mayan calendar. With things like the Lance Henricksen show Millennium, Rapture themed works and other media feeding/tapping into the same zeitgeist. It seems so silly now, but there were serious concerns about the Y2K bug wiping out computer systems as we know it, as well as other general hysteria. If there was any doubt about these themes White Wolf finished off each line with their end of the world coda book.<br /> <br /> \u200bWe still have apocalyptic memes in media and our society, but they seem to have shifted from the world will end to society collapsing/stagnating.Things like the housing crisis and the failure of big banks have shifted a lot of peoples concerns to a much more personal level. It's hard to worry about the end of the world when you are worried about the next mortgage payment. Yet, with all that there are so many things that feel like progress (even if they are heavily resisted in various arenas) that don't seem tied to the rampant consumerism of the 90s. Forms of Democracy have gotten a second wind (and the hit again) with things like the Arab Spring, gender and sexuality equality are much better than when I was a kid (although they still have a long way to go), Captain America is black and Thor is a woman. Many YouTube stars are banal glory seekers, but so many others are able to artistically flourish in a way never before because they control the platform and their message. It is a very paradoxical time (no pun intended).<br /> <br /> \u200bOne of the reasons that I shifted to Awakening (which to be fair has far less weighty philosophical underpinnings than Ascension) was a desire to move away from the nihilism inherent in the original game line. What I have read so far of M20 seems to have shifted away from that, which I am thankful for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see, thanks for explaining your standpoint!<br /> <br /> I agree with most of it, though, to be honest, the &quot;the end is niiiiiigh&quot; thing never was a big pert of <i>my </i>WoD, or a part of WoD I felt the most important. Honestly, the 10 minutes before the apocalypse thing always stroke me as silly. That's why I was a big fan of the cyclical Gehenna concept, when it came up and why I liked M20's stance on the ascension war than Revised's. So, that could be big part of why I never felt the games that out-of-time, even while I started playing them quite late. The apocalypses just never were the important part to me, in comparison to the other themes and plots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T08:19:40-07:00","id":1107020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1106085-mayo-vs-mustard?p=1106760#post1106760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, I see, thanks for explaining your standpoint!<br /> <br /> I agree with most of it, though, to be honest, the &quot;the end is niiiiiigh&quot; thing never was a big pert of <i>my </i>WoD, or a part of WoD I felt the most important. Honestly, the 10 minutes before the apocalypse thing always stroke me as silly. That's why I was a big fan of the cyclical Gehenna concept, when it came up and why I liked M20's stance on the ascension war than Revised's. So, that could be big part of why I never felt the games that out-of-time, even while I started playing them quite late. The apocalypses just never were the important part to me, in comparison to the other themes and plots.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bNo problem, I've been foot-in-mouth often enough that I appreciate and strive for clarifying discussions. I'm glad you avoided the nihilistic themes. I started with the first book (hopefully fight for reality), and got/read every book as it came out, so I literally ended with Ascension as the last book I read for the original run, so in my mind the entire line ended with the taint of Revised end of the world view point. It is what it is and like I said, I do appreciate M20s efforts to reset and its explicit freedom to choose you WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3385-ckobbe","name":"ckobbe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T14:15:39-07:00","id":1107118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ckobbe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1106085-mayo-vs-mustard?p=1107020#post1107020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bNo problem, I've been foot-in-mouth often enough that I appreciate and strive for clarifying discussions. I'm glad you avoided the nihilistic themes. I started with the first book (hopefully fight for reality), and got/read every book as it came out, so I literally ended with Ascension as the last book I read for the original run, so in my mind the entire line ended with the taint of Revised end of the world view point. It is what it is and like I said, I do appreciate M20s efforts to reset and its explicit freedom to choose you WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I might add I never read the ToJ books themselves. I've read some Wiki entries, but as a whole, it didn't interest me, really. Also, the sour pill of WoD's ending and NWoD was quite enough.<br /> <br /> Yea, I agree, the 20ths stance on it is good (and I'm quite nervous and hopeful at the same time about what WW will do in the future), although I somewhat missed the metaplot (ok, to be fair, V20 and W20 <i>has</i> some metaplot). i just don't think the metaplot have to end in an actual apocalypse, or that it has to end in the foreseeable future. That's why I didn't like the Revised-era's focus on the &quot;final nights&quot; because it had the presume of an actual, inevitable ending and that led to the death of my favorite games, fortunately, only temporarily.<br /> <br /> The other themes of the games I feel more-or-less actual even today (or even more so).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T15:22:48-07:00","id":1107135,"title":"","content":"I always felt that the &quot;apocalypse&quot; for Mage was somewhat forced. Mage hadn't this big prophecy about the End being near and unavoidable, no Gehena, no Apocalypse, nobody believed Mass Ascencion was something doable in a near future, and until late 2nd and Revised the issue it's never given importance. Ascencion had to happen to wrapp the cWoD metaplot, but not because it was important for the metaplot of Mage itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T13:07:02-07:00","id":1108120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1106085-mayo-vs-mustard?p=1107118#post1107118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, I might add I never read the ToJ books themselves. I've read some Wiki entries, but as a whole, it didn't interest me, really. Also, the sour pill of WoD's ending and NWoD was quite enough.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI haven't read V20 or W20 (so I can't judge them), but so far I have to say I am kind of glad that with the direction they were going they let the old MtAscension line die, then gave it room to breath and build nostalgia before rebooting the line. If the had tried it 15 years back it would have just felt like whiplash again instead of the modular toolkit we have now.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3385-ckobbe","name":"ckobbe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T16:12:06-07:00","id":1108182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ckobbe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1106085-mayo-vs-mustard?p=1108120#post1108120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI haven't read V20 or W20 (so I can't judge them), but so far I have to say I am kind of glad that with the direction they were going they let the old MtAscension line die, then gave it room to breath and build nostalgia before rebooting the line. If the had tried it 15 years back it would have just felt like whiplash again instead of the modular toolkit we have now.</div> </div> </div> </div>On that line, I'm even more worried about the fifth edition of Mage, than for Vampire's in regards of changing the setting into something entirely else. Revised was a bit too much and I have the itch that WW would go for a direction even more depressing. I hope not, in fact, I hope they'll use the &quot;New Millenium&quot; plotline from M20, but...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T06:45:38-07:00","id":1108380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">On that line, I'm even more worried about the fifth edition of Mage, than for Vampire's in regards of changing the setting into something entirely else. Revised was a bit too much and I have the itch that WW would go for a direction even more depressing. I hope not, in fact, I hope they'll use the &quot;New Millenium&quot; plotline from M20, but...</div> </div> </div> </div>MORE depressing than &quot;nobody won the war and nobody will because the world has ben lost to apathy, magick it's impossible to do without lengthy and highly dangerous rituals, 