img\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That bit of Mage was worse than depressing. Much of it was actively boring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 06-27-2017, 02:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T14:41:55-07:00","id":1108515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1106085-mayo-vs-mustard?p=1108182#post1108182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On that line, I'm even more worried about the fifth edition of Mage, than for Vampire's in regards of changing the setting into something entirely else. Revised was a bit too much and I have the itch that WW would go for a direction even more depressing. I hope not, in fact, I hope they'll use the &quot;New Millenium&quot; plotline from M20, but...</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSo wait, by my count we have 1st, 2nd, Revised (3rd), and M20 (4th), with a couple of side games. Is there a 5th edition on the horizon or is my count off?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3385-ckobbe","name":"ckobbe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T14:49:34-07:00","id":1108517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1106085-mayo-vs-mustard?p=1108380#post1108380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> MORE depressing than &quot;nobody won the war and nobody will because the world has ben lost to apathy, magick it's impossible to do without lengthy and highly dangerous rituals, everyone in the Umbra it's dead and no one should want to go there, Paradox it's worse than ever,better get a mundane job and forget about magick altogether&quot;.<br /> <br /> Hope not. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bExcept for the nobody wins the Ascension War (which I believe to be a fundamental impossibility since human actions/beliefs are as prone to chaos and unexpected evolution as any system out there), I see no reason to play with the other points mentioned. First, because thankfully, M20 is set up as a toolkit (admittedly with certain assumptions, but ones easily sidestepped), and second because I have 15 years of personal growth that I did not have at the end of the old line and am far more likely to mod/hack any system/setting to fit the themes/moods/goals of myself and my fellow gamers than I was in my much younger days.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3385-ckobbe","name":"ckobbe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T16:45:16-07:00","id":1108546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1106085-mayo-vs-mustard?p=1108380#post1108380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> MORE depressing than &quot;nobody won the war and nobody will because the world has ben lost to apathy, magick it's impossible to do without lengthy and highly dangerous rituals, everyone in the Umbra it's dead and no one should want to go there, Paradox it's worse than ever,better get a mundane job and forget about magick altogether&quot;.<br /> <br /> Hope not. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I hope too. As I said, I'd prefer the more uplift tone of the New Millenium from M20, I think it provides much more potential for interesting stories and reason to play the game. <br /> <br /> Although, theorizing on the worst case scenarion, somewhat based on the direction V5 seems taking and the talks about Werewolf:<br /> <br /> - the Technocracy truly won the war, it's absolutely omnipresent and near-omnipotent<br /> - the Umbra is just as far as in Revised, or more so and magic is as hard or even harder to do<br /> - the Traditions are basically scattered extremist terrorist cells, refusing to acknowledge their loss and gaining some surge from the extreme religous and political groups worldwide <br /> <br /> So, in a sense it could be very different from the crushing apathy of Revised and somewhat more close the 2nd ed, but cranked up to eleven and being, in the end, just as hopeless in tone as Revised was, just in a different way. But I truly hope it won't come to that and we don't know anything, I'm really just theorizing on the above mentined things and some snippets from Martin during the Tenebrae Noctis event a while ago.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ckobbe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1106085-mayo-vs-mustard?p=1108515#post1108515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bSo wait, by my count we have 1st, 2nd, Revised (3rd), and M20 (4th), with a couple of side games. Is there a 5th edition on the horizon or is my count off?</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said, we don't know anything and there isn't any talk about it from WW, but, if they won't fail hard with V5 and W5, I guess we'll eventally get M5 too.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T20:56:22-07:00","id":1108614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1106085-mayo-vs-mustard?p=1108546#post1108546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I said, we don't know anything and there isn't any talk about it from WW, but, if they won't fail hard with V5 and W5, I guess we'll eventally get M5 too.</div> </div> </div> </div>The One World of Darkness promotion trailer showed Magey things, as well as their presentation at the con in Berlin pretty much has shown Mage side-by-side with Vampire and Werewolf as one of the three main gamelines that makes up the One WoD to them. That and the Mage Prelude game they put out. So yeah. It's pretty much in the pipeline, but with zero info on it yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 06-28-2017, 03:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T08:34:03-07:00","id":1109778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1106085-mayo-vs-mustard?p=1108614#post1108614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The One World of Darkness promotion trailer showed Magey things, as well as their presentation at the con in Berlin pretty much has shown Mage side-by-side with Vampire and Werewolf as one of the three main gamelines that makes up the One WoD to them. That and the Mage Prelude game they put out. So yeah. It's pretty much in the pipeline, but with zero info on it yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bMan I really don't know how I feel about this, Onyx has what?, something like 30 game lines they are already managing, with years between releases of books in some of the lines. I love the quality and care that goes into most of the products, but kind of wish they would focus a little provide a steady stream of substantial products instead of spreading things so thin. I wonder how many people are like me and are only looking at a handful of game lines and are lucky to get one or two books a year. I have plenty of game lines that I only check up on every six months are so (and still find no change in status) already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3385-ckobbe","name":"ckobbe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T08:48:06-07:00","id":1118580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ckobbe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1106085-mayo-vs-mustard?p=1109778#post1109778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bMan I really don't know how I feel about this, Onyx has what?, something like 30 game lines they are already managing, with years between releases of books in some of the lines. I love the quality and care that goes into most of the products, but kind of wish they would focus a little provide a steady stream of substantial products instead of spreading things so thin. I wonder how many people are like me and are only looking at a handful of game lines and are lucky to get one or two books a year. I have plenty of game lines that I only check up on every six months are so (and still find no change in status) already.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind that V5, W5, M5, etc. are being produced by the new White Wolf Publishing, which is not the same as Onyx Path Publishing. Onyx Path has licensed the rights to produce 20th anniversary editions but is not currently (to the best of my knowledge) licensed to produce 5th Edition materials.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/693-thomasm","name":"ThomasM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar693_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}